# Scene
trueqbit with Claude (Opus 5.5), 2026-11-21: the symbol-level reading
of the coroutine types layer (result_box.h, fire_and_forget.h, task.h,
when_all.h).

# Decided
- trueqbit: Claude's leans and routing. #1630: async_task is one class
  template (d9d0e4d2), its promise split into task_promise<T> and its
  void specialization over task_promise_base<T>, since a promise cannot
  hold both return_value() and return_void(), constrained or not;
  async_when_all() keeps each task's outcome in a result_box
  (6bf53a1c), one start_one() template, no rethrow_first(). #1631: the
  void overload's doc-comment drops the storage's update() and remove().
- Claude: result_box's Intention changes in 6bf53a1c rather than on
  #1631: that commit makes async_when_all() one of its fillers.
- The two public async_when_all() overloads stay: a merged signature
  (conditional return type) would show in users' diagnostics.
- Nothing in the layer leaves its header; the preambles stay on their
  bearers.

# Discussed
- Merged down #1630 -> #1633 -> #1631 by merge commits, no conflicts.
  pre-commit.sh exits 0 before every commit. Not compiled.

